{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdV9FjmtXv69KQ5p5xiFUa","type":"tool_result","content":"costs\nlogs\nplan.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\n# Plan for #178\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\nDecisions: generator is **MkDocs Material** (nav, search and `mkdocs build --strict` link checking come built in; Hugo and Jekyll need more custom work for the same result). Pages live in `docs/site/`; `mkdocs.yml` is new at the repo root with `docs_dir: docs/site`. `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/layout.md` and `docs/TODO.md` stay outside the site and user pages link to the proposal by absolute GitHub URL (strict mode rejects links leaving `docs_dir`). The Gate 2 runbook is copied-by-move into the site (step 4).\n\n1. **Config key source of truth (new, `internal/config/keys.go`).** Add `func Keys() []string` returning every documented dotted key: the top-level keys, `intervals.*`, `intake.mode|label`, `merge.protected_paths`, `stale.*`, `redact.gitleaks.*`, `sidecars.<name>.repo|ref`, and the override keys (`every`, `max_open`, `group_size`, `autoclose`, `route`, `model`, `timeout`, `sidecar`, `after`, `plan_section`, `tests`, `max_test_fixes`, `max_review_rounds`, `reviewers`, `diff_warn_lines`, `diff_max_lines`, `agent`). Derive from the `yaml:` tags of `resolvedYAML` and `roleYAML` in `internal/config/render.go` by reflection, and add the input-only keys (`merge.protected_paths`, `overrides`) from the list parsed in `internal/config/raw.go`. Add `keys_test.go` that fails if a key parsed in `raw.go` is missing from `Keys()` (so the list cannot lag the loader). Reason: the docs check needs one list that tracks the code.\n2. **CLI command source (new, `internal/cli/commands.go`).** Add `func CommandPaths() []string` that walks `NewRoot(&App{})` and returns every command path (`ard serve`, `ard config check`, `ard labels sync`, `ard rebuild-state`, `ard init`, `ard version`) with each command's flag names (`--dry-run`, `--loops`, ...). No change to `NewRoot`.\n3. **Docs drift test (new package `internal/docscheck`, `docscheck_test.go`).** Read `docs/site/**/*.md` from the repo root (found by walking up to `go.mod`). Rules: (a) every inline or fenced `ard <words>` command that starts a line or an inline code span must resolve to a path in `cli.CommandPaths()`, and every `--flag` on that line must be a flag of that command or a global flag; (b) the page `docs/site/configuration.md` must list every `config.Keys()` entry as a backticked key in a table (undocumented key fails), and every backticked key in that table must be in `Keys()` (stale key fails). Lines can opt out with `<!-- docscheck:ignore -->` on the previous line. Pure Go, runs in `go test ./...`, so `make test` covers it.\n4. **Site scaffolding.** New `mkdocs.yml` (Material theme, `site_url: https://albertcbrown.github.io/ard/`, `docs_dir: docs/site`, `strict: true`, search plugin, nav listing the pages below). New `docs/site/requirements.txt` pinning `mkdocs` and `mkdocs-material` versions. Add `site/` to `.gitignore` (edit existing file). Move `docs/runbooks/gate-2.md` to `docs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md` with `git mv` and update any references (`grep -rn \"runbooks/gate-2\"`, including `docs/layout.md`, README and `docs/proposal.md`).\n5. **Write the pages** (`docs/site/`), each grounded in code and the proposal, with the proposal linked rather than copied:\n   - `index.md` Overview: loop (scanners, triage, worker, reviewers, merger), the `ard:` labels (from the proposal's Label state machine; check `internal/labels`), what humans still decide (approval, merges until the merger lands, protected paths).\n   - `getting-started.md`: create and install the GitHub App with the exact permissions (proposal Guardrails, Identity; #85), the ruleset bypass entry, `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` and the bot-commit workflow (point to `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` as the example and `internal/botcheck`), `ard init`, `ard labels sync`, `ard config check`, model credential (`internal/modelauth`), first `ard serve`, filing and labelling a first issue. Note git >= 2.47.0 and macOS/Linux only.\n   - `configuration.md`: table of every key with default (read defaults from `internal/config/defaults.go`), role directories, overrides, `intake`, `merge.protected_paths`, budgets, sidecars.\n   - `roles.md`: starter roles from `internal/roles/` (`ard init` set), writing a `prompt.txt`, the role-file frontmatter contract (keys `role`, `status`, `attempt`, `next`; see `internal/closeout`), the per-role write allowlist (proposal triage and worker sections).\n   - `operations.md`: kill switch (`paused` key, pause file), status issue, logs and state dir (`~/.ard`), Reaper and failure causes, usage limits (`internal/limits`), cost table (#172, `internal/costs`), waking loops (#161), upgrades, backups, rebuilding a damaged clone (proposal executor section), `ard rebuild-state`. Link `operations/gate-2-runbook.md`.\n   - `security.md`: no GitHub token in agents, untrusted input as files, redaction incl. host paths (#156, `internal/redact`), host mode vs Docker (#84), bot-commit audit.\n   - `troubleshooting.md`: GH013 ruleset rejections, git too old (#165), `ard:executor:failed` and how to retry, no-plan gate, `needs-human`.\n   - `install.md`: build from source with `make build`; leave a note that the Homebrew cask (#177) is added when it lands.\n6. **`make docs-check` target (edit `Makefile`).** The target runs `mkdocs build --strict -d /tmp/ard-site` (needs mkdocs on PATH; it does not install it) and `go test ./internal/docscheck/...`. Add to `.PHONY`. `make test` stays Go-only and already runs the drift test.\n7. **README and proposal.** README: replace the \"design stage\" status line's neighbourhood with a link to `https://albertcbrown.github.io/ard/` and add a Documentation link near the top. The proposal's Rollout already lists Phase 4 (verify, no edit needed). Update `docs/layout.md` with `docs/site/`, `mkdocs.yml`, `internal/docscheck/`.\n8. **Human follow-up document (new `docs/runbooks/pages-setup.md`, not in the site).** State exactly what a maintainer adds under `.github/` (agents cannot): (a) `.github/workflows/docs.yml`: trigger `push` to `main` with `paths: [docs/site/**, mkdocs.yml, internal/config/**, internal/cli/**]` plus `pull_request` with the same paths; job 1 sets up Python, `pip install -r docs/site/requirements.txt`, `mkdocs build --strict`, and `go test ./internal/docscheck/...`; on push to `main` a deploy job uses `actions/upload-pages-artifact` and `actions/deploy-pages` with `pages: write` and `id-token: write`. (b) Settings > Pages > Source: GitHub Actions. (c) Add the docs check to the required checks if wanted.\n\n### Test plan\n\nCommand: `make test` (runs `go test ./...`); also `make lint`; `make docs-check` when mkdocs is installed.\n\n- `TestKeysCoverRawParser` (`internal/config/keys_test.go`): every key the parser in `raw.go` accepts appears in `Keys()`. Failure case: a key added to the parser alone fails it.\n- `TestCommandPaths` (`internal/cli/commands_test.go`): expected paths include `ard config check`, `ard labels sync`, `ard serve` with `--loops`, `ard init`.\n- `TestDocsCommandsExist` (`internal/docscheck`): passes on the real docs. Cases using a temp docs dir: `ard bogus` fails; `ard serve --nope` fails; `ard serve --dry-run` passes; line preceded by the ignore comment passes.\n- `TestDocsConfigKeysMatch`: undocumented key in a fixture table fails with the key's name; stale documented key fails; the real `configuration.md` passes.\n- Manual (human, listed in the issue's done-when): follow Getting started on a scratch repo to a first triaged issue and note it in the PR; verify the live site after the maintainer adds the workflow.\n- Edge cases: commands in fenced blocks with `$ ` prompts or `\\` continuations; `ard` appearing in prose (only code spans and fenced blocks are checked).\n\n### Risk\n\nLow. No runtime code changes: two small read-only exported helpers in `internal/config` and `internal/cli`, a test package, docs and a Makefile target. None of `merge.protected_paths` is touched by the agent PR (no `.github/`, `.ard/config.yaml`, role dirs, Dockerfile, deploy/). The `Keys()` list is a new public (internal) interface that must track the loader; the step 1 test guards that. The deploy workflow, the Pages setting and the CI steps for the site build are a human follow-up (step 8). Documentation accuracy is the main residual risk and needs the manual scratch-repo run.\n\n### Size\n\nL, roughly 1,200 to 1,800 changed lines, almost all Markdown. If the worker finds it near diff_warn_lines, split: docs content first, then the site config and checks. Files touched: `mkdocs.yml` (new), `.gitignore`, `Makefile`, `README.md`, `docs/layout.md`, `docs/site/*.md` and `docs/site/requirements.txt` (new), `docs/runbooks/gate-2.md` (moved), `docs/runbooks/pages-setup.md` (new), `internal/config/keys.go` and `keys_test.go` (new), `internal/cli/commands.go` and `commands_test.go` (new), `internal/docscheck/docscheck_test.go` (new).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18fd3f36-35cc-4ded-af2c-3b11f3d9a6c1","uuid":"2cdc42eb-6f0f-4739-9617-51415e3614d1","timestamp":"2026-11-24T13:34:27.166Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"costs\nlogs\nplan.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\n# Plan for #178\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\nDecisions: generator is **MkDocs Material** (nav, search and `mkdocs build --strict` link checking come built in; Hugo and Jekyll need more custom work for the same result). Pages live in `docs/site/`; `mkdocs.yml` is new at the repo root with `docs_dir: docs/site`. `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/layout.md` and `docs/TODO.md` stay outside the site and user pages link to the proposal by absolute GitHub URL (strict mode rejects links leaving `docs_dir`). The Gate 2 runbook is copied-by-move into the site (step 4).\n\n1. **Config key source of